    "summary": "Connect web pages, navigate external websites, and jump to internal page sections.",
    "content": "# Lesson 06: Hyperlinks (a): Absolute vs Relative URLs, target='_blank', and Anchors\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 06** of the Front-End Developer HTML Track at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Hyperlinks (a): Absolute vs Relative URLs, target='_blank', and Anchors**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Web Standards\nConnect web pages, navigate external websites, and jump to internal page sections.\n\nHTML is the cornerstone of the World Wide Web. Writing valid, semantic, and well-structured HTML ensures your web pages look great, rank high in search engines, and remain accessible to everyone.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Live Code Playground\nTry running and modifying this HTML code in the **Web Dev Lab** playground:\n\n```html\n<!-- External link opening in new tab -->\n<a href=\"https://google.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Search Google</a>\n\n<!-- Relative internal link -->\n<a href=\"#section-contact\">Jump to Contact</a>\n\n<!-- Section anchor -->\n<h2 id=\"section-contact\">Contact Information</h2>\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Front-End Best Practice**: Always validate your HTML tags, close all open elements, and use semantic tags (<article>, <section>, <nav>) instead of excessive generic <div> containers!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nComplete this practical challenge:\n1. **Goal**: Build a table of contents with 3 anchor links that jump to corresponding sections on the same page.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Paste the code into the HTML tab, observe the live rendered preview, and check the interactive results!\n",
