    "summary": "Capture user data using form tags, text inputs, email inputs, and submit buttons.",
    "content": "# Lesson 10: HTML Forms Part 1: form, action, method, and Basic Inputs\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 10** of the Front-End Developer HTML Track at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **HTML Forms Part 1: form, action, method, and Basic Inputs**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Web Standards\nCapture user data using form tags, text inputs, email inputs, and submit buttons.\n\nHTML is the cornerstone of the World Wide Web. Writing valid, semantic, and well-structured HTML ensures your web pages look great, rank high in search engines, and remain accessible to everyone.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Live Code Playground\nTry running and modifying this HTML code in the **Web Dev Lab** playground:\n\n```html\n<form action=\"/submit-form\" method=\"POST\">\n  <label for=\"username\">Username:</label>\n  <input type=\"text\" id=\"username\" name=\"username\" required>\n  \n  <label for=\"useremail\">Email:</label>\n  <input type=\"email\" id=\"useremail\" name=\"useremail\" required>\n  \n  <button type=\"submit\">Register Now</button>\n</form>\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Front-End Best Practice**: Always validate your HTML tags, close all open elements, and use semantic tags (<article>, <section>, <nav>) instead of excessive generic <div> containers!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nComplete this practical challenge:\n1. **Goal**: Build a newsletter signup form with an email input, name input, and submit button.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Paste the code into the HTML tab, observe the live rendered preview, and check the interactive results!\n",
