    "summary": "Collect diverse inputs including numerical ranges, dates, options, and file attachments.",
    "content": "# Lesson 11: HTML Forms Part 2: Numbers, Dates, Checkboxes, Radio Buttons, and Files\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 11** of the Front-End Developer HTML Track at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **HTML Forms Part 2: Numbers, Dates, Checkboxes, Radio Buttons, and Files**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Web Standards\nCollect diverse inputs including numerical ranges, dates, options, and file attachments.\n\nHTML is the cornerstone of the World Wide Web. Writing valid, semantic, and well-structured HTML ensures your web pages look great, rank high in search engines, and remain accessible to everyone.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Live Code Playground\nTry running and modifying this HTML code in the **Web Dev Lab** playground:\n\n```html\n<!-- Radio buttons (mutually exclusive) -->\n<input type=\"radio\" id=\"student\" name=\"role\" value=\"student\" checked>\n<label for=\"student\">Student</label>\n\n<input type=\"radio\" id=\"teacher\" name=\"role\" value=\"teacher\">\n<label for=\"teacher\">Instructor</label>\n\n<!-- Checkbox -->\n<input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"terms\" name=\"terms\" required>\n<label for=\"terms\">I agree to terms and conditions</label>\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Front-End Best Practice**: Always validate your HTML tags, close all open elements, and use semantic tags (<article>, <section>, <nav>) instead of excessive generic <div> containers!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nComplete this practical challenge:\n1. **Goal**: Create an event registration form asking for attendee count (number), event date (date), and meal preference (radio).\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Paste the code into the HTML tab, observe the live rendered preview, and check the interactive results!\n",
