    "summary": "Organize complex form interfaces with multi-line textareas, select options, and fieldsets.",
    "content": "# Lesson 12: HTML Forms Part 3: textarea, Dropdown Selects, and fieldset Grouping\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 12** of the Front-End Developer HTML Track at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **HTML Forms Part 3: textarea, Dropdown Selects, and fieldset Grouping**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Web Standards\nOrganize complex form interfaces with multi-line textareas, select options, and fieldsets.\n\nHTML is the cornerstone of the World Wide Web. Writing valid, semantic, and well-structured HTML ensures your web pages look great, rank high in search engines, and remain accessible to everyone.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Live Code Playground\nTry running and modifying this HTML code in the **Web Dev Lab** playground:\n\n```html\n<fieldset>\n  <legend>Course Enrollment</legend>\n  <label for=\"courseSelect\">Choose Track:</label>\n  <select id=\"courseSelect\" name=\"course\">\n    <option value=\"python\">🐍 Python Automation</option>\n    <option value=\"frontend\">🌐 Front-End Web Development</option>\n    <option value=\"excel\">📊 Excel Masterclass</option>\n  </select>\n\n  <label for=\"bio\">Student Bio:</label>\n  <textarea id=\"bio\" name=\"bio\" rows=\"4\"></textarea>\n</fieldset>\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Front-End Best Practice**: Always validate your HTML tags, close all open elements, and use semantic tags (<article>, <section>, <nav>) instead of excessive generic <div> containers!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nComplete this practical challenge:\n1. **Goal**: Create a customer feedback form with a dropdown rating (1-5 stars) and a textarea for detailed comments.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Paste the code into the HTML tab, observe the live rendered preview, and check the interactive results!\n",
