    "content": "# Lesson 19: SEO Metadata, Open Graph (OG) Social Tags & Favicon Configuration\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 19** of the Front-End Developer HTML Track at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **SEO Metadata, Open Graph (OG) Social Tags & Favicon Configuration**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Web Standards\nOptimize your pages for Google search indexing and rich social media sharing cards.\n\nHTML is the cornerstone of the World Wide Web. Writing valid, semantic, and well-structured HTML ensures your web pages look great, rank high in search engines, and remain accessible to everyone.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Live Code Playground\nTry running and modifying this HTML code in the **Web Dev Lab** playground:\n\n```html\n<!-- Open Graph Facebook / LinkedIn / WhatsApp -->\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Bargisy eSchool | Web Development Path\">\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Master HTML5, CSS3, and JavaScript from scratch.\">\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://bargisy-eschool.com/cover.jpg\">\n<link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/x-icon\" href=\"/favicon.ico\">\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Front-End Best Practice**: Always validate your HTML tags, close all open elements, and use semantic tags (<article>, <section>, <nav>) instead of excessive generic <div> containers!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nComplete this practical challenge:\n1. **Goal**: Write the complete SEO head tags for an e-commerce product page (title, description, og:title, og:image).\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Paste the code into the HTML tab, observe the live rendered preview, and check the interactive results!\n",
