    "summary": "Target specific HTML elements using tag names, reusable classes, and unique IDs.",
    "content": "# Lesson 03: Basic CSS Selectors: Element, Class (.class), and ID (#id)\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 03** of the Front-End Developer CSS Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Basic CSS Selectors: Element, Class (.class), and ID (#id)**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Architecture\nTarget specific HTML elements using tag names, reusable classes, and unique IDs.\n\nCSS is the design language of the web. Understanding how browsers calculate styles, render layout trees, and handle modern responsive properties gives you the power to create breathtaking user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive CSS Sandbox\nReview the CSS snippet below and try it in the **Web Dev Lab**:\n\n```css\n/* Element selector */\np { font-size: 16px; }\n\n/* Class selector (reusable) */\n.btn-primary {\n  background-color: #2563eb;\n  color: white;\n  padding: 8px 16px;\n  border-radius: 8px;\n}\n\n/* ID selector (unique) */\n#main-header {\n  border-bottom: 2px solid #e2e8f0;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Modern CSS Best Practice**: Avoid magic numbers! Rely on responsive units (rem, em, clamp, %, fr), keep specificity low, and design mobile-first!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Style a primary button with a class and a hero banner with an ID selector.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your styles in the CSS editor tab and watch the live preview update instantly!\n",
