    "difficulty": "Beginner",
    "summary": "Master how browsers resolve conflicting styles using the cascade and specificity weighting.",
    "content": "# Lesson 06: The CSS Cascade, Inheritance & Rule Specificity Calculation\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 06** of the Front-End Developer CSS Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **The CSS Cascade, Inheritance & Rule Specificity Calculation**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Architecture\nMaster how browsers resolve conflicting styles using the cascade and specificity weighting.\n\nCSS is the design language of the web. Understanding how browsers calculate styles, render layout trees, and handle modern responsive properties gives you the power to create breathtaking user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive CSS Sandbox\nReview the CSS snippet below and try it in the **Web Dev Lab**:\n\n```css\n/* Specificity: Element (1) < Class (10) < ID (100) < Inline (1000) */\np { color: black; }           /* Specificity: 0,0,1 */\n.highlight { color: blue; }   /* Specificity: 0,1,0 */\n#special { color: red; }      /* Specificity: 1,0,0 (Wins!) */\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Modern CSS Best Practice**: Avoid magic numbers! Rely on responsive units (rem, em, clamp, %, fr), keep specificity low, and design mobile-first!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Calculate the specificity score of 'header nav ul.menu li a.active'.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your styles in the CSS editor tab and watch the live preview update instantly!\n",
    "tags": "CSS, Front-End, Lesson 06, Web Design, Beginner",
