    "category_name": "Modern CSS & Design",
    "difficulty": "Beginner",
    "summary": "Understand why modern responsive typography and spacing rely on rem and relative units.",
    "content": "# Lesson 10: CSS Units: Absolute (px) vs Relative Units (rem, em, %, vh, vw)\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 10** of the Front-End Developer CSS Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **CSS Units: Absolute (px) vs Relative Units (rem, em, %, vh, vw)**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Architecture\nUnderstand why modern responsive typography and spacing rely on rem and relative units.\n\nCSS is the design language of the web. Understanding how browsers calculate styles, render layout trees, and handle modern responsive properties gives you the power to create breathtaking user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive CSS Sandbox\nReview the CSS snippet below and try it in the **Web Dev Lab**:\n\n```css\nhtml { font-size: 16px; } /* 1rem = 16px */\n\nbody {\n  font-size: 1rem;       /* 16px */\n  margin: 0;\n  min-height: 100vh;     /* 100% viewport height */\n}\n\n.container {\n  width: 90%;            /* 90% of parent */\n  max-width: 1200px;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Modern CSS Best Practice**: Avoid magic numbers! Rely on responsive units (rem, em, clamp, %, fr), keep specificity low, and design mobile-first!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Convert a design specification from fixed pixels (24px, 32px) to rem units.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your styles in the CSS editor tab and watch the live preview update instantly!\n",
    "tags": "CSS, Front-End, Lesson 10, Web Design, Beginner",
    "read_time": 5,
    "author": "Mohammed Bargisy",
    "status": "published",
    "views": 380,
    "cover_gradient": "linear-gradient(135deg, #0284c7, #06b6d4)",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-14 12:10:00"
