    "difficulty": "Beginner",
    "summary": "Visualize how every HTML element is rendered as a rectangular box with 4 distinct layers.",
    "content": "# Lesson 11: The CSS Box Model: Margin, Border, Padding, and Content\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 11** of the Front-End Developer CSS Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **The CSS Box Model: Margin, Border, Padding, and Content**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Architecture\nVisualize how every HTML element is rendered as a rectangular box with 4 distinct layers.\n\nCSS is the design language of the web. Understanding how browsers calculate styles, render layout trees, and handle modern responsive properties gives you the power to create breathtaking user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive CSS Sandbox\nReview the CSS snippet below and try it in the **Web Dev Lab**:\n\n```css\n.box {\n  width: 300px;\n  /* Content inside */\n  padding: 20px;       /* Spacing inside border */\n  border: 2px solid #2563eb;\n  margin: 15px auto;   /* Spacing outside border, centered horizontally */\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Modern CSS Best Practice**: Avoid magic numbers! Rely on responsive units (rem, em, clamp, %, fr), keep specificity low, and design mobile-first!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Draw or code a card demonstrating clear margin, border, and padding separation.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your styles in the CSS editor tab and watch the live preview update instantly!\n",
