    "category_name": "Modern CSS & Design",
    "difficulty": "Beginner",
    "summary": "Eliminate layout calculation headaches by making padding and borders count inside total width.",
    "content": "# Lesson 12: The box-sizing Property: content-box vs border-box\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 12** of the Front-End Developer CSS Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **The box-sizing Property: content-box vs border-box**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Architecture\nEliminate layout calculation headaches by making padding and borders count inside total width.\n\nCSS is the design language of the web. Understanding how browsers calculate styles, render layout trees, and handle modern responsive properties gives you the power to create breathtaking user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive CSS Sandbox\nReview the CSS snippet below and try it in the **Web Dev Lab**:\n\n```css\n/* The Gold Standard Universal Reset */\n*, *::before, *::after {\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n}\n\n.box-reliable {\n  width: 250px;\n  padding: 25px; /* Total rendered width remains exactly 250px! */\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Modern CSS Best Practice**: Avoid magic numbers! Rely on responsive units (rem, em, clamp, %, fr), keep specificity low, and design mobile-first!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Compare two 300px divs: one with content-box and one with border-box, both having 20px padding.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your styles in the CSS editor tab and watch the live preview update instantly!\n",
    "tags": "CSS, Front-End, Lesson 12, Web Design, Beginner",
