    "summary": "Learn why vertical margins collapse together and how auto margins center block elements.",
    "content": "# Lesson 13: CSS Margin Mastery: Margin Collapse & Centering with margin: auto\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 13** of the Front-End Developer CSS Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **CSS Margin Mastery: Margin Collapse & Centering with margin: auto**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Architecture\nLearn why vertical margins collapse together and how auto margins center block elements.\n\nCSS is the design language of the web. Understanding how browsers calculate styles, render layout trees, and handle modern responsive properties gives you the power to create breathtaking user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive CSS Sandbox\nReview the CSS snippet below and try it in the **Web Dev Lab**:\n\n```css\n.centered-block {\n  width: 80%;\n  max-width: 600px;\n  margin-left: auto;\n  margin-right: auto; /* Centers element perfectly */\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Modern CSS Best Practice**: Avoid magic numbers! Rely on responsive units (rem, em, clamp, %, fr), keep specificity low, and design mobile-first!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Center a card horizontally on the page using max-width and margin: auto.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your styles in the CSS editor tab and watch the live preview update instantly!\n",
