    "summary": "Design sharp borders and understand how outlines differ by not occupying box model space.",
    "content": "# Lesson 15: Borders: Styles (solid, dashed, dotted), Widths, and Outline\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 15** of the Front-End Developer CSS Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Borders: Styles (solid, dashed, dotted), Widths, and Outline**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Architecture\nDesign sharp borders and understand how outlines differ by not occupying box model space.\n\nCSS is the design language of the web. Understanding how browsers calculate styles, render layout trees, and handle modern responsive properties gives you the power to create breathtaking user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive CSS Sandbox\nReview the CSS snippet below and try it in the **Web Dev Lab**:\n\n```css\n.input-box {\n  border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;\n  outline: none;\n}\n.input-box:focus {\n  outline: 2px solid #3b82f6; /* Focus ring without shifting layout */\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Modern CSS Best Practice**: Avoid magic numbers! Rely on responsive units (rem, em, clamp, %, fr), keep specificity low, and design mobile-first!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Create an interactive input field with a distinct border on blur and glowing outline on focus.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your styles in the CSS editor tab and watch the live preview update instantly!\n",
