    "content": "# Lesson 17: Typography Part 2: Loading Google Fonts with @import and <link>\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 17** of the Front-End Developer CSS Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Typography Part 2: Loading Google Fonts with @import and <link>**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Architecture\nIncorporate custom typography like Inter, Roboto, or Poppins from Google Fonts.\n\nCSS is the design language of the web. Understanding how browsers calculate styles, render layout trees, and handle modern responsive properties gives you the power to create breathtaking user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive CSS Sandbox\nReview the CSS snippet below and try it in the **Web Dev Lab**:\n\n```css\n<!-- In HTML <head> -->\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n<link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;600;700&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n\n<style>\n  body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; }\n</style>\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Modern CSS Best Practice**: Avoid magic numbers! Rely on responsive units (rem, em, clamp, %, fr), keep specificity low, and design mobile-first!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Import Google Font 'Poppins' with weights 400 and 700 and apply to all headings.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your styles in the CSS editor tab and watch the live preview update instantly!\n",
