    "summary": "Align text (left, right, center, justify), uppercase titles, and remove anchor underlines.",
    "content": "# Lesson 19: Text Alignment & Direction: text-align, text-transform, and text-decoration\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 19** of the Front-End Developer CSS Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Text Alignment & Direction: text-align, text-transform, and text-decoration**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Architecture\nAlign text (left, right, center, justify), uppercase titles, and remove anchor underlines.\n\nCSS is the design language of the web. Understanding how browsers calculate styles, render layout trees, and handle modern responsive properties gives you the power to create breathtaking user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive CSS Sandbox\nReview the CSS snippet below and try it in the **Web Dev Lab**:\n\n```css\na {\n  text-decoration: none; /* Removes default link underline */\n  color: #2563eb;\n}\na:hover {\n  text-decoration: underline;\n}\n\n.card-title {\n  text-align: center;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Modern CSS Best Practice**: Avoid magic numbers! Rely on responsive units (rem, em, clamp, %, fr), keep specificity low, and design mobile-first!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Create an elegant navbar link with no default underline, adding an underline effect on hover.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your styles in the CSS editor tab and watch the live preview update instantly!\n",
