    "summary": "Decorate containers with responsive hero background images.",
    "content": "# Lesson 20: Background Colors and Background Images (url, repeat, size, position)\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 20** of the Front-End Developer CSS Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Background Colors and Background Images (url, repeat, size, position)**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Architecture\nDecorate containers with responsive hero background images.\n\nCSS is the design language of the web. Understanding how browsers calculate styles, render layout trees, and handle modern responsive properties gives you the power to create breathtaking user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive CSS Sandbox\nReview the CSS snippet below and try it in the **Web Dev Lab**:\n\n```css\n.hero {\n  background-image: url('https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1517694712202-14dd9538aa97?w=1200');\n  background-size: cover;          /* Scales image to cover container */\n  background-position: center;     /* Centers focal point */\n  background-repeat: no-repeat;\n  min-height: 400px;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Modern CSS Best Practice**: Avoid magic numbers! Rely on responsive units (rem, em, clamp, %, fr), keep specificity low, and design mobile-first!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Create a hero banner with a background cover image that stays centered on window resize.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your styles in the CSS editor tab and watch the live preview update instantly!\n",
