    "summary": "Generate vivid linear color transitions for buttons, cards, and banners.",
    "content": "# Lesson 21: Multi-Stop Linear Gradients: syntax, angles (to right, 135deg)\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 21** of the Front-End Developer CSS Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Multi-Stop Linear Gradients: syntax, angles (to right, 135deg)**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Architecture\nGenerate vivid linear color transitions for buttons, cards, and banners.\n\nCSS is the design language of the web. Understanding how browsers calculate styles, render layout trees, and handle modern responsive properties gives you the power to create breathtaking user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive CSS Sandbox\nReview the CSS snippet below and try it in the **Web Dev Lab**:\n\n```css\n.gradient-btn {\n  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #2563eb, #7c3aed);\n  color: white;\n  border: none;\n  padding: 10px 24px;\n  border-radius: 12px;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Modern CSS Best Practice**: Avoid magic numbers! Rely on responsive units (rem, em, clamp, %, fr), keep specificity low, and design mobile-first!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Build a multi-stop linear gradient blending from teal to deep blue at a 45-degree angle.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your styles in the CSS editor tab and watch the live preview update instantly!\n",
