    "summary": "Create circular spotlight gradients and color wheel conic effects.",
    "content": "# Lesson 22: Radial and Conic Gradients in Modern CSS\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 22** of the Front-End Developer CSS Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Radial and Conic Gradients in Modern CSS**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Architecture\nCreate circular spotlight gradients and color wheel conic effects.\n\nCSS is the design language of the web. Understanding how browsers calculate styles, render layout trees, and handle modern responsive properties gives you the power to create breathtaking user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive CSS Sandbox\nReview the CSS snippet below and try it in the **Web Dev Lab**:\n\n```css\n.spotlight {\n  background: radial-gradient(circle at center, #3b82f6, #0f172a);\n}\n.pie-chart {\n  background: conic-gradient(#3b82f6 0% 40%, #10b981 40% 70%, #f59e0b 70% 100%);\n  border-radius: 50%;\n  width: 150px; height: 150px;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Modern CSS Best Practice**: Avoid magic numbers! Rely on responsive units (rem, em, clamp, %, fr), keep specificity low, and design mobile-first!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Create a 3-color pie chart badge using a single conic-gradient on a circular div.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your styles in the CSS editor tab and watch the live preview update instantly!\n",
