    "summary": "Craft modern UI curves, avatar circles, and pill-shaped badges.",
    "content": "# Lesson 23: Border Radius Mastery: Rounded Corners, Circles & Pill Shapes\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 23** of the Front-End Developer CSS Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Border Radius Mastery: Rounded Corners, Circles & Pill Shapes**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Architecture\nCraft modern UI curves, avatar circles, and pill-shaped badges.\n\nCSS is the design language of the web. Understanding how browsers calculate styles, render layout trees, and handle modern responsive properties gives you the power to create breathtaking user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive CSS Sandbox\nReview the CSS snippet below and try it in the **Web Dev Lab**:\n\n```css\n.avatar {\n  width: 80px; height: 80px;\n  border-radius: 50%; /* Perfect circle */\n  object-fit: cover;\n}\n\n.pill-badge {\n  border-radius: 9999px; /* Pill capsule */\n  padding: 4px 12px;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Modern CSS Best Practice**: Avoid magic numbers! Rely on responsive units (rem, em, clamp, %, fr), keep specificity low, and design mobile-first!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Design a pill-shaped tag badge with rounded corners that never distort regardless of text length.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your styles in the CSS editor tab and watch the live preview update instantly!\n",
