    "title": "Lesson 28: Controlling Element Visibility: display: none vs visibility: hidden",
    "slug": "css-lesson-28-controlling-element-visibility-display-none-vs-visibility-hidden",
    "category": "programming",
    "track": "css",
    "track_name": "CSS3 Track",
    "category_name": "Modern CSS & Design",
    "difficulty": "Beginner",
    "summary": "Understand the key difference: display: none removes the element from layout; visibility: hidden hides it while preserving space.",
    "content": "# Lesson 28: Controlling Element Visibility: display: none vs visibility: hidden\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 28** of the Front-End Developer CSS Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Controlling Element Visibility: display: none vs visibility: hidden**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Architecture\nUnderstand the key difference: display: none removes the element from layout; visibility: hidden hides it while preserving space.\n\nCSS is the design language of the web. Understanding how browsers calculate styles, render layout trees, and handle modern responsive properties gives you the power to create breathtaking user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive CSS Sandbox\nReview the CSS snippet below and try it in the **Web Dev Lab**:\n\n```css\n.hidden-removed { display: none; }        /* No space reserved */\n.hidden-collapsed { visibility: hidden; } /* Space reserved in flow */\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Modern CSS Best Practice**: Avoid magic numbers! Rely on responsive units (rem, em, clamp, %, fr), keep specificity low, and design mobile-first!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Create a toggle demonstration showing layout shift with display: none vs preservation with visibility: hidden.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your styles in the CSS editor tab and watch the live preview update instantly!\n",
    "tags": "CSS, Front-End, Lesson 28, Web Design, Beginner",
