    "difficulty": "Beginner",
    "summary": "Remove ugly default bullets and design clean navigational lists.",
    "content": "# Lesson 30: Styling Lists: list-style-type, list-style-position, and Custom Bullets\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 30** of the Front-End Developer CSS Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Styling Lists: list-style-type, list-style-position, and Custom Bullets**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Architecture\nRemove ugly default bullets and design clean navigational lists.\n\nCSS is the design language of the web. Understanding how browsers calculate styles, render layout trees, and handle modern responsive properties gives you the power to create breathtaking user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive CSS Sandbox\nReview the CSS snippet below and try it in the **Web Dev Lab**:\n\n```css\nul.clean-list {\n  list-style: none; /* Remove default bullets */\n  padding: 0;\n  margin: 0;\n}\nul.clean-list li {\n  padding: 8px 0;\n  border-bottom: 1px solid #f1f5f9;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Modern CSS Best Practice**: Avoid magic numbers! Rely on responsive units (rem, em, clamp, %, fr), keep specificity low, and design mobile-first!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Build an elegant feature checklist where each item has a custom checkmark icon instead of standard bullets.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your styles in the CSS editor tab and watch the live preview update instantly!\n",
