    "summary": "Understand how browsers render block elements on new lines versus inline elements that flow with text.",
    "content": "# Lesson 31: CSS Display Property: block, inline, and inline-block\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 31** of the Front-End Developer CSS Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **CSS Display Property: block, inline, and inline-block**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Architecture\nUnderstand how browsers render block elements on new lines versus inline elements that flow with text.\n\nCSS is the design language of the web. Understanding how browsers calculate styles, render layout trees, and handle modern responsive properties gives you the power to create breathtaking user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive CSS Sandbox\nReview the CSS snippet below and try it in the **Web Dev Lab**:\n\n```css\n.block-elem { display: block; width: 100%; }\n.inline-elem { display: inline; /* width/height ignored */ }\n.inline-block-elem { display: inline-block; width: 120px; }\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Modern CSS Best Practice**: Avoid magic numbers! Rely on responsive units (rem, em, clamp, %, fr), keep specificity low, and design mobile-first!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Align 3 buttons horizontally using inline-block with explicit padding and widths.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your styles in the CSS editor tab and watch the live preview update instantly!\n",
