    "summary": "Pin navigation headers, floating action buttons (FAB), and cookie banners to the browser viewport.",
    "content": "# Lesson 35: CSS Positioning: fixed (Pinned to the Viewport)\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 35** of the Front-End Developer CSS Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **CSS Positioning: fixed (Pinned to the Viewport)**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Architecture\nPin navigation headers, floating action buttons (FAB), and cookie banners to the browser viewport.\n\nCSS is the design language of the web. Understanding how browsers calculate styles, render layout trees, and handle modern responsive properties gives you the power to create breathtaking user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive CSS Sandbox\nReview the CSS snippet below and try it in the **Web Dev Lab**:\n\n```css\n.floating-chat-btn {\n  position: fixed;\n  bottom: 24px;\n  right: 24px;\n  width: 56px; height: 56px;\n  border-radius: 50%;\n  background-color: #2563eb;\n  color: white;\n  box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.4);\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Modern CSS Best Practice**: Avoid magic numbers! Rely on responsive units (rem, em, clamp, %, fr), keep specificity low, and design mobile-first!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Build a 'Back to Top' floating action button fixed to the bottom-right of the screen that remains visible when scrolling.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your styles in the CSS editor tab and watch the live preview update instantly!\n",
