    "difficulty": "Beginner",
    "summary": "Wipe out erratic browser defaults (margins, paddings) for consistent cross-browser rendering.",
    "content": "# Lesson 45: CSS Normalization & The Universal Box Model Reset\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 45** of the Front-End Developer CSS Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **CSS Normalization & The Universal Box Model Reset**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Architecture\nWipe out erratic browser defaults (margins, paddings) for consistent cross-browser rendering.\n\nCSS is the design language of the web. Understanding how browsers calculate styles, render layout trees, and handle modern responsive properties gives you the power to create breathtaking user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive CSS Sandbox\nReview the CSS snippet below and try it in the **Web Dev Lab**:\n\n```css\n*, *::before, *::after {\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n}\nimg, picture, video {\n  display: block;\n  max-width: 100%;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Modern CSS Best Practice**: Avoid magic numbers! Rely on responsive units (rem, em, clamp, %, fr), keep specificity low, and design mobile-first!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Include a modern 5-line CSS reset at the top of your stylesheet and test in multiple browsers.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your styles in the CSS editor tab and watch the live preview update instantly!\n",
    "tags": "CSS, Front-End, Lesson 45, Web Design, Beginner",
