    "summary": "Master modern two-dimensional CSS Grid layout: css grid introduction: two-dimensional layout power vs flexbox.",
    "content": "# Lesson 61: CSS Grid Introduction: Two-Dimensional Layout Power vs Flexbox\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 61** of the Front-End Developer CSS Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **CSS Grid Introduction: Two-Dimensional Layout Power vs Flexbox**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Architecture\nMaster modern two-dimensional CSS Grid layout: css grid introduction: two-dimensional layout power vs flexbox.\n\nCSS is the design language of the web. Understanding how browsers calculate styles, render layout trees, and handle modern responsive properties gives you the power to create breathtaking user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive CSS Sandbox\nReview the CSS snippet below and try it in the **Web Dev Lab**:\n\n```css\n.grid-layout {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));\n  gap: 20px;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Modern CSS Best Practice**: Avoid magic numbers! Rely on responsive units (rem, em, clamp, %, fr), keep specificity low, and design mobile-first!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Implement a responsive layout utilizing css grid introduction: two-dimensional layout power vs flexbox.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your styles in the CSS editor tab and watch the live preview update instantly!\n",
