    "content": "# Lesson 85: Container Query Units (cqw, cqh) for True Modular Component Sizing\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 85** of the Front-End Developer CSS Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Container Query Units (cqw, cqh) for True Modular Component Sizing**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & Architecture\nBuild adaptable, responsive interfaces across all screen sizes: container query units (cqw, cqh) for true modular component sizing.\n\nCSS is the design language of the web. Understanding how browsers calculate styles, render layout trees, and handle modern responsive properties gives you the power to create breathtaking user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive CSS Sandbox\nReview the CSS snippet below and try it in the **Web Dev Lab**:\n\n```css\n@media (min-width: 768px) {\n  .responsive-box {\n    /* Tablet & Desktop styles */\n    font-size: clamp(1rem, 2vw + 0.5rem, 1.5rem);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Modern CSS Best Practice**: Avoid magic numbers! Rely on responsive units (rem, em, clamp, %, fr), keep specificity low, and design mobile-first!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Test responsive adaptability on mobile and desktop viewports demonstrating container query units (cqw, cqh) for true modular component sizing.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your styles in the CSS editor tab and watch the live preview update instantly!\n",
