    "content": "# Lesson 02: Connecting JavaScript: Script Tags (<script src='...'>) and defer vs async\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 02** of the Front-End Developer JavaScript Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Connecting JavaScript: Script Tags (<script src='...'>) and defer vs async**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & JavaScript Runtime\nLearn where to place script tags and how defer guarantees HTML parsing before execution.\n\nJavaScript is the world's most versatile programming language, powering billions of interactive websites, web applications, and servers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive Code Implementation\nStudy and run this JavaScript code in the **Web Dev Lab** or browser console:\n\n```javascript\n<!-- Best Practice: external script in head with defer -->\n<script src=\"js/app.js\" defer></script>\n\n<script>\n  // Inline script runs after DOM is ready\n  console.log(\"DOM loaded safely.\");\n</script>\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **JavaScript Pro Tip**: Always use === for strict comparisons, declare variables with const and let (never var), and catch asynchronous errors with try/catch!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Explain the difference between <script defer> and <script async> for page performance.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Switch to the JS tab, run your code, and check the integrated console drawer for outputs and logs!\n",
