    "content": "# Lesson 03: The Developer Console: console.log(), console.warn(), console.error(), and console.table()\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 03** of the Front-End Developer JavaScript Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **The Developer Console: console.log(), console.warn(), console.error(), and console.table()**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & JavaScript Runtime\nMaster browser debugging tools to inspect variables, output warnings, and render structured table data.\n\nJavaScript is the world's most versatile programming language, powering billions of interactive websites, web applications, and servers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive Code Implementation\nStudy and run this JavaScript code in the **Web Dev Lab** or browser console:\n\n```javascript\nconsole.log(\"Standard log information\");\nconsole.warn(\"⚠️ Warning: low memory warning simulated\");\nconsole.error(\"❌ Critical: failed to fetch API data\");\n\nconst students = [\n  { name: \"Mohammed\", score: 98 },\n  { name: \"Sara\", score: 95 }\n];\nconsole.table(students); // Formatted visual table!\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **JavaScript Pro Tip**: Always use === for strict comparisons, declare variables with const and let (never var), and catch asynchronous errors with try/catch!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Log a list of 3 course objects using console.table() in the console.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Switch to the JS tab, run your code, and check the integrated console drawer for outputs and logs!\n",
