    "content": "# Lesson 10: Template Literals: Modern String Interpolation with Backticks\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 10** of the Front-End Developer JavaScript Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Template Literals: Modern String Interpolation with Backticks**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & JavaScript Runtime\nEliminate messy string concatenation with multiline backticks and ${expression} syntax.\n\nJavaScript is the world's most versatile programming language, powering billions of interactive websites, web applications, and servers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive Code Implementation\nStudy and run this JavaScript code in the **Web Dev Lab** or browser console:\n\n```javascript\nconst user = \"Mohammed\";\nconst role = \"Lead Engineer\";\nconst projects = 14;\n\nconst greeting = `Hello, ${user}!\nYou are currently signed in as: ${role.toUpperCase()}.\nActive Projects: ${projects + 2}.`;\n\nconsole.log(greeting);\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **JavaScript Pro Tip**: Always use === for strict comparisons, declare variables with const and let (never var), and catch asynchronous errors with try/catch!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Format a multi-line invoice receipt using template literals with calculated subtotals inside ${}.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Switch to the JS tab, run your code, and check the integrated console drawer for outputs and logs!\n",
