    "content": "# Lesson 11: String Properties & Methods: .length, .toUpperCase(), .toLowerCase(), .trim()\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 11** of the Front-End Developer JavaScript Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **String Properties & Methods: .length, .toUpperCase(), .toLowerCase(), .trim()**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & JavaScript Runtime\nInspect string length, sanitize inputs, and normalize casing.\n\nJavaScript is the world's most versatile programming language, powering billions of interactive websites, web applications, and servers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive Code Implementation\nStudy and run this JavaScript code in the **Web Dev Lab** or browser console:\n\n```javascript\nconst rawEmail = \"   Student@Bargisy-eSchool.COM   \";\nconst cleanEmail = rawEmail.trim().toLowerCase();\nconsole.log(\"Sanitized Email:\", cleanEmail);\nconsole.log(\"Character length:\", cleanEmail.length);\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **JavaScript Pro Tip**: Always use === for strict comparisons, declare variables with const and let (never var), and catch asynchronous errors with try/catch!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Write a function that accepts messy user input, strips leading/trailing spaces, and converts it to lowercase.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Switch to the JS tab, run your code, and check the integrated console drawer for outputs and logs!\n",
