    "summary": "Locate characters and test for substrings with modern ES6 boolean methods.",
    "content": "# Lesson 12: Searching Strings: .includes(), .startsWith(), .endsWith(), and .indexOf()\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 12** of the Front-End Developer JavaScript Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Searching Strings: .includes(), .startsWith(), .endsWith(), and .indexOf()**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & JavaScript Runtime\nLocate characters and test for substrings with modern ES6 boolean methods.\n\nJavaScript is the world's most versatile programming language, powering billions of interactive websites, web applications, and servers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive Code Implementation\nStudy and run this JavaScript code in the **Web Dev Lab** or browser console:\n\n```javascript\nconst filename = \"financial-report-2026.xlsx\";\n\nconsole.log(filename.endsWith(\".xlsx\"));     // true\nconsole.log(filename.startsWith(\"financial\")); // true\nconsole.log(filename.includes(\"2026\"));        // true\nconsole.log(filename.indexOf(\"-\"));            // 9\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **JavaScript Pro Tip**: Always use === for strict comparisons, declare variables with const and let (never var), and catch asynchronous errors with try/catch!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Validate an image upload filename: ensure it contains a hyphen and ends with .png or .jpg.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Switch to the JS tab, run your code, and check the integrated console drawer for outputs and logs!\n",
