    "difficulty": "Beginner",
    "summary": "Direct program execution dynamically based on varying runtime inputs.",
    "content": "# Lesson 16: Conditional Statements: if, else if, and else Branches\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 16** of the Front-End Developer JavaScript Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Conditional Statements: if, else if, and else Branches**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & JavaScript Runtime\nDirect program execution dynamically based on varying runtime inputs.\n\nJavaScript is the world's most versatile programming language, powering billions of interactive websites, web applications, and servers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive Code Implementation\nStudy and run this JavaScript code in the **Web Dev Lab** or browser console:\n\n```javascript\nconst score = 88;\nlet letterGrade;\n\nif (score >= 90) {\n  letterGrade = \"A\";\n} else if (score >= 80) {\n  letterGrade = \"B\";\n} else if (score >= 70) {\n  letterGrade = \"C\";\n} else {\n  letterGrade = \"F\";\n}\nconsole.log(`Grade: ${letterGrade}`);\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **JavaScript Pro Tip**: Always use === for strict comparisons, declare variables with const and let (never var), and catch asynchronous errors with try/catch!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Implement an admission fee calculator: children <12 pay $5, adults pay $15, seniors >65 pay $10.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Switch to the JS tab, run your code, and check the integrated console drawer for outputs and logs!\n",
    "tags": "JavaScript, Front-End, Lesson 16, Coding, Beginner",
