    "summary": "Write concise, single-line conditional assignments without verbose if blocks.",
    "content": "# Lesson 17: The Ternary Operator: Inline (condition ? exprIfTrue : exprIfFalse)\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 17** of the Front-End Developer JavaScript Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **The Ternary Operator: Inline (condition ? exprIfTrue : exprIfFalse)**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & JavaScript Runtime\nWrite concise, single-line conditional assignments without verbose if blocks.\n\nJavaScript is the world's most versatile programming language, powering billions of interactive websites, web applications, and servers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive Code Implementation\nStudy and run this JavaScript code in the **Web Dev Lab** or browser console:\n\n```javascript\nconst userRole = \"admin\";\nconst dashboard = userRole === \"admin\" ? \"Full Access Dashboard\" : \"Restricted View\";\nconsole.log(dashboard);\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **JavaScript Pro Tip**: Always use === for strict comparisons, declare variables with const and let (never var), and catch asynchronous errors with try/catch!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Assign a shippingFee variable ($0 if orderTotal > $100, otherwise $15) using a ternary operator.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Switch to the JS tab, run your code, and check the integrated console drawer for outputs and logs!\n",
