    "summary": "Run loops based on variable conditions and ensure at least one execution with do-while.",
    "content": "# Lesson 23: While Loops and Do-While Loops: Condition-Controlled Execution\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 23** of the Front-End Developer JavaScript Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **While Loops and Do-While Loops: Condition-Controlled Execution**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & JavaScript Runtime\nRun loops based on variable conditions and ensure at least one execution with do-while.\n\nJavaScript is the world's most versatile programming language, powering billions of interactive websites, web applications, and servers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive Code Implementation\nStudy and run this JavaScript code in the **Web Dev Lab** or browser console:\n\n```javascript\nlet attempts = 0;\nwhile (attempts < 3) {\n  attempts++;\n  console.log(`Attempt ${attempts}: Trying server connection...`);\n}\n\nlet x = 10;\ndo {\n  console.log(\"Runs at least once regardless of condition!\");\n} while (x < 5);\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **JavaScript Pro Tip**: Always use === for strict comparisons, declare variables with const and let (never var), and catch asynchronous errors with try/catch!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Simulate a coin flip until getting 3 consecutive heads using a while loop.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Switch to the JS tab, run your code, and check the integrated console drawer for outputs and logs!\n",
