    "id": "js-24",
    "lesson_number": 24,
    "title": "Lesson 24: Loop Controls: break to Exit Immediately & continue to Skip Iteration",
    "slug": "js-lesson-24-loop-controls-break-to-exit-immediately-continue-to-skip-iteration",
    "category": "programming",
    "track": "javascript",
    "track_name": "JavaScript Track",
    "category_name": "JavaScript Development",
    "difficulty": "Beginner",
    "summary": "Control loop execution dynamically by breaking early on target matches or skipping steps.",
    "content": "# Lesson 24: Loop Controls: break to Exit Immediately & continue to Skip Iteration\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 24** of the Front-End Developer JavaScript Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Loop Controls: break to Exit Immediately & continue to Skip Iteration**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & JavaScript Runtime\nControl loop execution dynamically by breaking early on target matches or skipping steps.\n\nJavaScript is the world's most versatile programming language, powering billions of interactive websites, web applications, and servers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive Code Implementation\nStudy and run this JavaScript code in the **Web Dev Lab** or browser console:\n\n```javascript\nfor (let i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {\n  if (i % 2 === 0) continue; // Skip evens\n  if (i === 7) {\n    console.log(\"Target 7 found, terminating loop!\");\n    break;\n  }\n  console.log(`Odd number: ${i}`);\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **JavaScript Pro Tip**: Always use === for strict comparisons, declare variables with const and let (never var), and catch asynchronous errors with try/catch!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Iterate through a list of filenames, skip any ending in .tmp, and stop immediately if finding 'virus.exe'.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Switch to the JS tab, run your code, and check the integrated console drawer for outputs and logs!\n",
    "tags": "JavaScript, Front-End, Lesson 24, Coding, Beginner",
    "read_time": 5,
    "author": "Mohammed Bargisy",
    "status": "published",
    "views": 358,
    "cover_gradient": "linear-gradient(135deg, #d97706, #f59e0b)",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-14 12:15:00"
