    "summary": "Iterate directly over values without maintaining manual counter variables.",
    "content": "# Lesson 25: The for...of Loop: Clean Iteration over Arrays, Strings, and Iterables\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 25** of the Front-End Developer JavaScript Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **The for...of Loop: Clean Iteration over Arrays, Strings, and Iterables**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & JavaScript Runtime\nIterate directly over values without maintaining manual counter variables.\n\nJavaScript is the world's most versatile programming language, powering billions of interactive websites, web applications, and servers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive Code Implementation\nStudy and run this JavaScript code in the **Web Dev Lab** or browser console:\n\n```javascript\nconst fruits = [\"Apple\", \"Mango\", \"Banana\", \"Orange\"];\nfor (const fruit of fruits) {\n  console.log(`🍎 Fruit: ${fruit}`);\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **JavaScript Pro Tip**: Always use === for strict comparisons, declare variables with const and let (never var), and catch asynchronous errors with try/catch!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Iterate over a string 'Bargisy' with for...of and print each character uppercase.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Switch to the JS tab, run your code, and check the integrated console drawer for outputs and logs!\n",
