    "content": "# Lesson 31: Function Declarations vs Function Expressions: Syntax & Hoisting Differences\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 31** of the Front-End Developer JavaScript Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Function Declarations vs Function Expressions: Syntax & Hoisting Differences**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & JavaScript Runtime\nMaster fundamental JavaScript mechanics: function declarations vs function expressions: syntax & hoisting differences.\n\nJavaScript is the world's most versatile programming language, powering billions of interactive websites, web applications, and servers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive Code Implementation\nStudy and run this JavaScript code in the **Web Dev Lab** or browser console:\n\n```javascript\nfunction calculateTotal(subtotal, tax = 0.15) {\n  return subtotal * (1 + tax);\n}\nconsole.log(\"Total:\", calculateTotal(100));\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **JavaScript Pro Tip**: Always use === for strict comparisons, declare variables with const and let (never var), and catch asynchronous errors with try/catch!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Implement a practical coding solution demonstrating function declarations vs function expressions: syntax & hoisting differences.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Switch to the JS tab, run your code, and check the integrated console drawer for outputs and logs!\n",
