    "content": "# Lesson 81: Event Delegation: Managing 100 List Items with a Single Parent Listener\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 81** of the Front-End Developer JavaScript Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Event Delegation: Managing 100 List Items with a Single Parent Listener**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concept & JavaScript Runtime\nCapture and respond to user interactions in real-time: event delegation: managing 100 list items with a single parent listener.\n\nJavaScript is the world's most versatile programming language, powering billions of interactive websites, web applications, and servers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive Code Implementation\nStudy and run this JavaScript code in the **Web Dev Lab** or browser console:\n\n```javascript\nconst btn = document.querySelector(\"#submitBtn\");\nbtn?.addEventListener(\"click\", (e) => {\n  e.preventDefault();\n  console.log(\"Button clicked safely!\");\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **JavaScript Pro Tip**: Always use === for strict comparisons, declare variables with const and let (never var), and catch asynchronous errors with try/catch!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. **Goal**: Build an interactive event handler demonstrating event delegation: managing 100 list items with a single parent listener.\n2. Open the **Interactive Web Dev Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Switch to the JS tab, run your code, and check the integrated console drawer for outputs and logs!\n",
